# Manual test of the local server API with the VS Code extension.
# Start the server without a browser, so the one-time link stays unused:
#
#   scripts/run.sh --no-browser
#
# The server prints a line like
#   Open http://127.0.0.1:8080/#token=<64 characters> in your browser (it works once, for 2 minutes).
# Put the 64 characters after "#token=" into the file tests/manual/api/.env (Git ignores it), as
#   TBR_LINK_TOKEN=<64 characters>
# The file local_api.env.example shows the format.

@port = 8080
@token = {{$dotenv TBR_LINK_TOKEN}}

### 1. The placeholder page (no login needed)
GET http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}/

### 2. Log in with the link token: 204 and a Set-Cookie header (a second try gives 401)
POST http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}/api/session
Origin: http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}
X-TaxBroker: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{"token":"{{token}}"}

### 3. Am I logged in? 204 after step 2, 401 before it
GET http://127.0.0.1:{{port}}/api/session
X-TaxBroker: 1
